irectory is still the workspace root, so `path.join(process.cwd(), \"dist\")` resolves correctly. However, if `NODE_ENV` isn\'t set to \"production\", the server logic gets the `createViteServer` section executed. This might cause issues, as the `createViteServer` call needs to resolve its dependencies.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now update `server.ts` to use a more stable environment detection logic. Since the development server runs `server.ts` directly, and the production server runs the bundled `dist/server.cjs` (which only exists after a successful build alongside `dist/index.html`), we can check if `dist/index.html` exists inside the workspace directory. This avoids any issues if `process.env.NODE_ENV` is not correctly propagated by the container host environment. Let\'s make this edit."
