ot going to work in production since the import was deleted. I will explore why this change occurred.\n\n\n**Confirming Vite Asset Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on validating my hypothesis regarding Vite\'s asset handling. I\'m confirming that the hardcoded image path, `/src/assets/images/gyden_heng_1779443461362.png`, will break in production as I suspected, since the build process won\'t copy the image. I have also confirmed that importing the image using a relative path, such as `../assets/images/gyden_heng_1779443461362.png`, and using the imported variable as the image source will allow Vite to bundle it correctly. However, a deeper look at the user\'s messages suggests this might not be the complete issue, and there may be a rendering issue.\n\n\n**Verifying Image Source**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on confirming the image source within `Hero.tsx`. I recall the user reported seeing a \"mock\" image, and I need to pinpoint which image is being rendered. I\'ve re-examined the directory listing and I can see the user\'s uploaded image. I\'ll need to carefully examine the `Hero.tsx` file for the exact image path being used. The directory listing shows that the image is named `gyden_heng_1779443461362.png`. The listing also shows the upload image is named the same, `gyden_heng_1779443461362.png` and both exist within `/src/assets/images`.\n\n\n**Investigating Element Issues**\n\nI\'m now investigating a user report about a broken `div` above the image. The user stated \"and the div above the image is broke\". I\'ve analyzed the code snippet provided, focusing on the `div` element at line 121 within the `Hero.tsx` component. The user described a broken `div`, and I\'ll need to assess the styling and structure. I am checking the classes, which include `bg-gradient-to-b`, `border`, `rounded-2xl`, and `shadow-xl`, to see if there is a conflict.\n\n\n**Clarifying Component Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now investigating the component hierarchy and the relationship between the `div`